## Overview

This document defines the standards for YOM frontend development. YOM has two Next.js frontend applications:

- **admin** — Next.js App Router, MUI v5, Azure AD (MSAL) auth. Runs on port **3002**.
- **b2b** — Next.js 16, React 19, MUI v7, Cypress E2E. Runs on port **3006**.

Both apps share the same conventions described in this document.

---

## Technology Stack

### Core Technologies
- **Framework**: Next.js App Router (admin) / Next.js 16 (b2b)
- **Language**: TypeScript — strict mode required for all files
- **UI Library**: Material UI (MUI) — v5 in admin, v7 in b2b
- **Package manager**: npm

### State Management & Data Flow
- **Server state**: SWR (`swr`) — caching, revalidation, loading/error states
- **Local state**: React `useState` / `useReducer` — component-level only
- **Global client state**: React Context — no Zustand, no Redux
- **Forms**: react-hook-form (via minimals components integration)

### Testing Framework
- **Unit & Component**: Jest + React Testing Library
- **E2E**: Cypress (b2b)
- **Coverage threshold**: 80% on component logic (business logic in hooks/services)

### HTTP Client
- **Axios** — two configured instances:
  - **v3 instance**: routes through `yom-gateway` (new path)
  - **legacy instance**: routes through `yom-api`
- All API calls are centralized in the service layer — components never call Axios directly

### Authentication
- **admin**: MSAL (Azure AD) — context-based auth via `@azure/msal-react`
- **b2b**: session/context-based auth

