## Project Structure

### Next.js App (admin / b2b)
```
src/
├── app/                     # Next.js App Router pages and layouts
│   ├── (auth)/              # Route groups
│   ├── layout.tsx           # Root layout
│   └── page.tsx             # Home page
├── components/              # UI components
│   ├── sections/            # Feature views (client components, page-level)
│   ├── ui/                  # Reusable primitives (buttons, cards, inputs)
│   └── minimals/            # Base components (react-hook-form, iconify integration)
├── hooks/                   # SWR domain hooks (useBanners, useCustomer, etc.)
├── services/                # Axios API service layer
├── lib/                     # Utility functions, constants, configs
├── types/                   # Shared TypeScript types and interfaces
└── styles/                  # Global styles
cypress/
└── e2e/                     # E2E tests organized by feature
```

### Component Layer Responsibilities
- **`sections/`**: Full feature views — composed of ui/ primitives + hooks. These are `'use client'` components.
- **`ui/`**: Pure UI atoms and molecules — reusable across sections. Minimal business logic.
- **`minimals/`**: Integration layer for react-hook-form and iconify — wraps third-party primitives with YOM conventions.

