## Component Conventions

### Functional Components Only
- Always use functional components with hooks
- No class components in new code

### Component Composition
- **`ui/`**: Basic, reusable UI elements — use MUI as foundation
- **`sections/`**: Complex feature views composed from ui/ — one section per major page area
- **`minimals/`**: Third-party integration wrappers — not to be modified frequently

### Props
- Destructure props in the function signature
- Provide default values for optional props
- Never pass raw objects without a defined type

```typescript
const ActionButton: React.FC<ActionButtonProps> = ({
  children,
  variant = 'contained',
  disabled = false,
  onClick,
}) => { /* ... */ };
```

### Error and Loading States
Every component that fetches data must handle all three states:

```typescript
const BannerList: React.FC = () => {
  const { data: banners, isLoading, error } = useBanners(customerId);

  if (isLoading) return <CircularProgress />;
  if (error) return <Alert severity="error">Failed to load banners</Alert>;
  if (!banners?.length) return <Typography>No banners found</Typography>;

  return (
    <Stack spacing={2}>
      {banners.map(b => <BannerCard key={b.id} banner={b} />)}
    </Stack>
  );
};
```

