## State Management

### Server State (SWR)
Use SWR for all server data — it handles caching, revalidation, and loading/error states. Domain hooks live in `src/hooks/`.

```typescript
// hooks/useBanners.ts
import useSWR from 'swr';
import { bannerService } from '@/services/bannerService';

export function useBanners(customerId: string) {
  return useSWR(['banners', customerId], () => bannerService.getAll(customerId));
}

export function useBanner(id: string) {
  return useSWR(id ? ['banner', id] : null, () => bannerService.getById(id));
}
```

**SWR conventions:**
- Key format: `[resourceName, ...params]` — enables targeted revalidation
- Pass `null` as key to conditionally skip fetching (e.g., when id is undefined)
- Use `mutate` from `useSWR` or global `mutate` to invalidate after mutations
- Set `revalidateOnFocus: false` in global SWR config where appropriate

```typescript
// After a mutation — invalidate related keys
const { mutate } = useBanners(customerId);
await bannerService.update(id, data);
mutate(); // revalidates the banners list
```

### Local State
- Use `useState` for simple component-level state
- Use `useReducer` for complex state with multiple sub-values
- Extract complex stateful logic into custom hooks

### Global Client State (React Context)
Use React Context for app-wide client state (auth, theme preferences, UI toggles). No Zustand, no Redux.

```typescript
// contexts/AuthContext.tsx
type AuthContextValue = {
  user: User | null;
  isAuthenticated: boolean;
  logout: () => void;
};

export const AuthContext = createContext<AuthContextValue | null>(null);

export function useAuth(): AuthContextValue {
  const ctx = useContext(AuthContext);
  if (!ctx) throw new Error('useAuth must be used within AuthProvider');
  return ctx;
}
```

### Forms (react-hook-form)
Use react-hook-form via the `minimals/` integration layer. Validation can use built-in rules or a resolver.

```typescript
import { useForm } from 'react-hook-form';

type BannerFormData = {
  title: string;
  url: string;
  active: boolean;
};

const BannerForm: React.FC = () => {
  const { register, handleSubmit, formState: { errors, isSubmitting } } = useForm<BannerFormData>();

  const onSubmit = async (data: BannerFormData) => {
    await bannerService.create(data);
  };

  return (
    <form onSubmit={handleSubmit(onSubmit)}>
      <TextField
        {...register('title', { required: 'Title is required' })}
        error={!!errors.title}
        helperText={errors.title?.message}
        label="Title"
      />
      <Button type="submit" disabled={isSubmitting}>Save</Button>
    </form>
  );
};
```

