## API Communication

### Service Layer
Centralize all API calls in `src/services/`. Components and hooks never call Axios directly.

```typescript
// services/bannerService.ts
import { axiosV3Instance } from '@/lib/axios'; // yom-gateway path

export const bannerService = {
  getAll: async (customerId: string): Promise<Banner[]> => {
    const response = await axiosV3Instance.get(`/customers/${customerId}/banners`);
    return response.data;
  },

  getById: async (id: string): Promise<Banner> => {
    const response = await axiosV3Instance.get(`/banners/${id}`);
    return response.data;
  },

  create: async (data: CreateBannerDto): Promise<Banner> => {
    const response = await axiosV3Instance.post('/banners', data);
    return response.data;
  },

  update: async (id: string, data: Partial<Banner>): Promise<Banner> => {
    const response = await axiosV3Instance.patch(`/banners/${id}`, data);
    return response.data;
  },

  remove: async (id: string): Promise<void> => {
    await axiosV3Instance.delete(`/banners/${id}`);
  },
};
```

### Axios Instances
Two instances are configured in `src/lib/axios.ts`:

- **`axiosV3Instance`**: base URL points to `yom-gateway` — use for all new endpoints
- **`axiosLegacyInstance`**: base URL points to `yom-api` — use only for endpoints not yet migrated

Always prefer the v3 instance for new service files.

### Hook + Service Pattern
The hook layer owns the SWR key and delegates data fetching to the service:

```
Component → useBanners() hook → SWR → bannerService.getAll() → Axios → yom-gateway
```

