## UI/UX Standards

### Material UI (MUI)
All styling is done with MUI — no Tailwind CSS, no custom CSS-in-JS outside MUI's `sx` prop.

```typescript
// sx prop for one-off styles
<Box sx={{ display: 'flex', gap: 2, alignItems: 'center', p: 3 }}>
  <Typography variant="h6" sx={{ fontWeight: 600 }}>
    Banners
  </Typography>
</Box>

// Stack for flex layouts
<Stack direction="row" spacing={2} alignItems="center">
  <Button variant="contained">Save</Button>
  <Button variant="outlined">Cancel</Button>
</Stack>

// Grid for responsive layouts
<Grid container spacing={3}>
  <Grid item xs={12} md={6}>
    <BannerCard banner={banner} />
  </Grid>
</Grid>
```

**MUI conventions:**
- Prefer MUI `spacing` units (multiples of 8px) over raw pixel values in `sx`
- Use theme tokens (`theme.palette`, `theme.typography`) instead of hardcoded colors/sizes
- Extend the theme in `src/lib/theme.ts` — never override MUI styles via global CSS

### Accessibility
- Use semantic HTML (`nav`, `main`, `article`, `button`) — not `div` for interactive elements
- Every interactive element must have an `aria-label` if purpose is not clear from visible text
- Keyboard navigation must work for all interactive elements
- Images must have `alt` text

### Loading & Feedback
- Show loading state during async operations — use MUI `CircularProgress` or `Skeleton`
- Show success/error feedback after form submissions — use MUI `Alert` or `Snackbar`
- Disable submit buttons during loading to prevent double-submit

